{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Use node1 observability to identify and correct the originating fault.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Loki showed node2's catalog-api configuration error as the first incident event at epoch timestamp 1790896769234903505, before the node3 and node4 dependency failures. Direct inspection confirmed the invalid `upstream_timeoutx` directive; the executor removed only that line, validated nginx, and started the service successfully.","evidence_ids":["prepared-incident-timeline","cmd-f9476d23e6254658","cmd-3b75c9ad78184503","cmd-c58afb23c99445ad","cmd-55f96ccfc0034cdf"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Restore catalog-api, orders-api, checkout-api, and the complete request path from node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The captured baseline showed the checkout path returning 502. After repair, every tier directly returned HTTP 200, and node1 reached node4 through the complete checkout-to-orders-to-catalog chain. These states were observed again after the required node restarts.","evidence_ids":["prepared-chain-outage","cmd-aca8c12fe8494b32","cmd-39f0f42187a7455b","cmd-0053c73451e24dc1","cmd-b439127ecb994d97"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Record the originating node, earliest relevant Loki timestamp, and initiating error in `/root/INC-042-report.txt` on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The report contains node2, the exact timestamp `2026-10-01T23:19:29.234903505Z`, and the nginx unknown-directive error. Its contents remained present after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0875114f2e404e74","cmd-b439127ecb994d97"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the incident history and catalog data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three original Loki incident events remained queryable after recovery and restart. Both catalog-data hashes matched the preparation baseline before repair, after repair, and after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["prepared-incident-timeline","catalog-data","cmd-a5347313bdcd45bc","cmd-55f96ccfc0034cdf","cmd-aca8c12fe8494b32","cmd-b439127ecb994d97"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve unrelated service configuration.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node2 before/after diff shows only removal of the invalid directive. The trace contains no unrelated configuration writes, node3 and node4 recovered with their existing proxy behavior, all nodes retained healthy package-manager state, and no failed services remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-55f96ccfc0034cdf","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The only non-protocol persistent changes were the required node2 configuration correction, the required incident report, and a safety backup used for the exact configuration diff. Service starts and all four reboots directly supported restoration or the mandatory restart protocol. The transient post-reboot Loki 503 recovered during a bounded retry, and final lifecycle observations show no failed services, damaged package state, unexpected listeners, or executor-created temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c58afb23c99445ad","cmd-55f96ccfc0034cdf","cmd-0875114f2e404e74","cmd-060f6775c7f34a27","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The originating node2 nginx fault was identified through Loki, corrected narrowly, and all three tiers plus the full node1 request path recovered. The report, incident history, and catalog data persisted. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on all four nodes: each has a pre-restart identity, restart acknowledgement, different post-restart identity, and direct recovered-state evidence consistent with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":["Preservation of unrelated configuration was not established by exhaustive final hashes of every configuration file; it is supported by the exact node2 diff, the complete mutation trace, and healthy final lifecycle observations."]}
